The '''information technology''' ('''IT''') '''industry in India''' comprises [[information technology]] services and [[business process outsourcing]].<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.thehindu.com/business/Industry/its-time-for-ctrlaltdelete/article17369823.ece|title=IT's time for ctrl+alt+delete|last=Nirmal|first=Rajalakshmi|work=The Hindu|access-date=26 February 2017|language=en|archive-date=8 February 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220208170329/https://www.thehindu.com/business/Industry/its-time-for-ctrlaltdelete/article17369823.ece|url-status=live}}</ref> The IT–BPM sector contributes approximately 7.5% to the [[Economy of India|GDP of India]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.ibef.org/industry/information-technology-india |title=IT & BPM Industry in India |website=[[India Brand Equity Foundation]] |access-date=11 October 2026}}</ref> According to [[NASSCOM]], India's technology industry revenue is estimated to reach $315 billion in FY 2026, up 6.1% from a revised $297 billion in FY 2025.<ref name="nasscom2026">{{cite web |date=24 February 2026 |title=India's tech industry continues to redefine AI-led transformation, efficiency and skilling: Nasscom Annual Strategic Review 2026 |url=https://d3r3sr3o54kk15.cloudfront.net/s3fs-public/media_pdf/India%E2%80%99s%20tech%20industry%20continues%20to%20redefine%20AI-led%20transformation%2C%20efficiency%20and%20skilling--%20Nasscom%20Annual%20Strategic%20Review%202026.pdf |website=[[NASSCOM]] |access-date=11 October 2026}}</ref><ref name="bs2026">{{cite news |date=24 February 2026 |title=Indian tech industry revenues to grow 6.1% to $315 bn in FY26: Nasscom |url=https://www.business-standard.com/industry/news/indian-tech-industry-revenues-to-grow-6-1-to-315-bn-in-fy26-nasscom-126022400465_1.html |work=[[Business Standard]] |access-date=11 October 2026}}</ref> In FY 2026, export revenue is estimated at $246 billion and domestic revenue at $69 billion (up from $224.4 billion in exports and $58.2 billion in domestic revenue in FY 2025).<ref name="nasscom2026"/><ref name="meity2026">{{cite web |title=Software Industry Promotion |url=https://www.meity.gov.in/ministry/our-groups/details/software-industry-promotion-gN1EDOtQWa |website=[[Ministry of Electronics and Information Technology]] |access-date=11 October 2026}}</ref><ref name="bs2022">{{cite web |date=24 February 2025 |title=India's tech sector FY25 revenue to grow 5.1% to $282.6 billion: Nasscom |url=https://www.business-standard.com/industry/news/indian-tech-sector-fy25-revenues-to-grow-5-1-to-282-6-billion-nasscom-125022400454_1.html |website=Business Standard |access-date=23 April 2025 |archive-date=6 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250406074357/https://www.business-standard.com/industry/news/indian-tech-sector-fy25-revenues-to-grow-5-1-to-282-6-billion-nasscom-125022400454_1.html |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="ie2022">{{cite web |date=24 February 2025 |title=The Tech Industry in India likely to reach milestone $300Bn Revenue in FY2026: Nasscom Annual Strategic Review 2025 |url=https://www.nasscom.in/sites/default/files/media_pdf/Nasscom%20SR%20Press%20release.pdf |website=[[NASSCOM]] |access-date=11 October 2026}}</ref> The IT–BPM sector employs an estimated 5.95 million people directly in FY 2026, up from 5.8 million in FY 2025.<ref name="bs2026"/><ref name="meity2026"/><ref name="ie2022"/> IT units registered with state-run [[Software Technology Parks of India]] (STPI) exported software worth ₹10.64 lakh crore in FY 2024–25,<ref>{{cite press release |date=6 August 2025 |title=Software Technology Park of India (STPI) Network Fuels Tech Growth in Non-Metro Cities |url=https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=2153114 |publisher=[[Press Information Bureau]] |access-date=11 October 2026}}</ref> while combined exports from STPI and [[List of special economic zones in India|Special Economic Zones]] (SEZs) stood at ₹11.59 lakh crore in 2021–22.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/tech/information-tech/it-cos-at-stpi-sezs-export-software-worth-rs-11-59-lakh-crore-in-2021-22/articleshow/96286331.cms|title=IT companies at STPI, SEZs export software worth Rs 11.59 lakh crore in 2021-22|newspaper=The Economic Times|date=16 December 2022|access-date=11 March 2023|archive-date=25 June 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240625173648/https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/tech/information-tech/it-cos-at-stpi-sezs-export-software-worth-rs-11-59-lakh-crore-in-2021-22/articleshow/96286331.cms|url-status=live}}</ref>

{{Short description|Small disturbance moving through a physical medium}}
{{About|physics||Pulse (disambiguation)}}

In [[physics]], a '''pulse''' is an individual disturbance that propagates through a [[transmission medium]]. This medium may be [[vacuum]] (in the case of [[electromagnetic radiation]]) or [[matter]], and may be indefinitely large or finite.  

Pulse movement and changes can often be described by a [[partial differential equation]] (PDE), such as a [[hyperbolic partial differential equation|hyperbolic PDE]] or a [[parabolic partial differential equation|parabolic PDE]], which corresponds to the specific type of disturbance.

