 |bibcode = 2006ChJAA...6..635Z 
|doi-access=free 
 }}</ref> 
Chronicles of the contemporary Europeans are more vague when consulted for supernovae candidates.<ref name=murdin>{{cite book |first1=Paul |last1=Murdin |first2=Lesley |last2=Murdin |year=1985 |title=Supernovae |publisher=Cambridge University Press |isbn=0-521-30038-X |url-access=registration |url=https://archive.org/details/supernovae00murd }}</ref> Whether this was due to the weather or other reasons, astronomers have questioned why the remnant attributed to Chinese observations of a guest star in AD 1054 (see [[SN 1054]]) is missing from the European records.<ref name=murdin/>

